speechtext:
1. Resolved, That it is expedient to amend The Inland Revenue Act, as amended by chapter six of the Statutes of 1914, and chapter twenty-eight of the Statutes of 1918 by repealing subsections (e), (f), (g) and t.h) of section two hundred and seventy-nine thereof and substituting therefor the following :-
279 (e) On cigars of all descriptions, made from raw leaf tobacco, three dollars per thousand ;
(f)	On all cigars when put uo in packages containing less than ten cigars each, four dollars per thousand;
(g)	On cigarette® made from ra,v leaf tobacco or any substitute therefor, weighing not more than three pounds per thousand, seven dollars and fifty cents per thousand ;
(h)	On cigarettes made from raw leaf tobacco or any substitute therefor, weighing more than three pounds per thousand, twelve dollars and fifty cents, per thousand ;
